WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.030
No one here is running half-assed!

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.610
Excuse me.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.530
Kakeru. We're not done talking.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:13.740
Prince.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.080
If you're only able to achieve
the same time at the next meet,

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.670
will you quit the team?

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:28.250
What?

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.710
Please. For the team.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.970
<b><i>Run with the Wind</i></b>

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.850
No way!

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:10.880
He said that?

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.070
That kind of talk is ineffective.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.030
I told you.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.320
Is he serious?

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.110
It's true that he went too far, though.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:25.970
Well, he is fast.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:32.000
He also said that because he's
taking running at Hakone seriously.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.750
Prince, you don't need to worry about it,

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.380
and I don't want the two of you
to have any weird biases.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.540
Don't tell anyone else.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.840
Okay.

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:45.700
We know he's not a bad guy.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.810
But he can be really irritable.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.720
I was so upset, I was up all night reading.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:55.210
You mean comics, right.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.640
Yes, I mean comics.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.280
<b><i>Mismatched Runners</i></b>

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.780
There's rice left over.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.920
Someone besides Kakeru isn't eating.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.060
I wonder how it'll actually go.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:17.670
Do you think I can achieve
the required official record?

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:20.640
Your time is improving.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:32.900
I enjoy running with you. I really do.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:39.070
Running next to you makes me feel like
I can reconsider what it means to run.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:43.430
Right foot forward, left foot forward.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:45.390
Slowly increasing your speed.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:47.790
You used to walk,

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:50.170
but before you know it,
it looks like you're running.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:54.510
I'm re-experiencing the excitement of running.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.210
I don't think I understand.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:03.220
But I think I understand what
it means to do something together.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:09.230
We read the same comics
together at the same time.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.810
We count down to start reading.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:17.620
There's a moment our waves become synchronized.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:22.190
We start turning the page simultaneously.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.800
The temperature in our rooms definitely
increases by one—no, two degrees.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.450
Even if we don't share our thoughts,

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:35.920
it feels like we've thoroughly
discussed the content.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:39.380
I see.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.620
I don't think I understand.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.820
Of course you don't.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.260
<b>Kansei University</b>

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.260
What?

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:49.010
Did he really say that?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.970
Didn't he say that to Prince?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.690
Yeah. He asked Prince to quit the team.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.480
Yeah.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.520
Quit the team?

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.050
He can't suddenly achieve an official record.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.150
Right?

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.740
Then it's decided.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:10.620
Prince is the first dropout.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.080
No, wait. Nothing's been decided yet.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.260
Haiji would never accept that.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:19.040
What did Haiji have to say about it?

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.280
Uh...

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.240
Don't worry about it.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:26.010
Don't have any weird biases.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.170
Don't tell anyone else.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.580
Wait, wait, wait!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.820
Joji, you mentioned it first!

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.970
It wasn't me! It was you!

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:37.230
You guys are such idiots.

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:45.640
You don't have to do 
anything to get hungry, huh?

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.460
There you are.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.690
Stop following me!

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.660
You tried to hide in the last
place I'd look for you.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.960
It got a little cold during
the time it took to find you.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.250
Come on. Eat up.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.970
I don't want it!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:44.210
It doesn't look good for a grown-ass man
to accept a lunch from another grown-ass man!

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:48.000
Don't worry about how it looks.
My presentation is perfect.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.930
That's not what I meant!

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.540
I knew something was off.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.800
I could tell not enough rice was missing.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:59.060
When I checked, I found exactly
one serving hadn't been eaten.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:01.340
You sure are looking closely.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.780
Of course I am.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:07.990
I consider the volume and nutrition everyone
needs when preparing meals everyday.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:12.630
Seriously?

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:15.080
Seriously.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:16.950
Since when?

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:21.420
Since I started cooking all our meals.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.960
That was four years ago.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:25.980
Has it been that long?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:29.580
Don't panic.

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:32.120
You don't have to push yourself so hard.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.510
You'll probably get it eventually.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.660
You won't say I definitely will, huh?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:41.650
Eating this will change my point of view.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.070
Come on. At least take
your mind off it with this.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.340
You're making it worse.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.320
Go, go!

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:53.520
You can do it!

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.740
That's it!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.180
You can do it!

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.200
Oh, wow!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.910
Yuki's time has improved a ton.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:02.440
Everyone's time might improve.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.530
Yeah.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.950
Bring it home!

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.950
A little more!

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:07.330
You can do it!

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:10.520
Yuki, final spurt!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:12.260
<b>Kurahara Kakeru 5000m Time</b>

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.640
It's going well.

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:25.340
It's only been three weeks,

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:28.530
but because you all stuck
to the training schedule,

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.320
we're starting to see results.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.530
Tomorrow's track meet will be a good
opportunity for a second chance.

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:39.740
Right now, we're working hard
to get into the Hakone Ekiden.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.650
Without even one of us, we can't get there.

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:43.960
We don't have any substitutes.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:48.670
Let's all attend tomorrow's track meet,
so we can all participate together.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:53.890
I'll now announce the members who will
be participating in tomorrow's track meet.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.630
What?

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.340
Huh? What? It's not everyone?

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:00.310
It's everyone. We'll all go.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.020
Running isn't everything.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:09.440
Running in tomorrow's track meet will be Musa,

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.670
Shindo,

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.320
Jota, Joji,

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.780
and Yuki.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:14.860
Those five.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.280
The remaining members 
will be going to the meet, as well.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.390
<b>Kikui University</b>

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.350
<b>42nd 
Kikui University 
Track and Field Meet</b>

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.350
<b>No 
unauthorized 
access to field
</b>Kikui University

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.650
They're not here.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.820
What's that strong team called?

00:09:56.820 --> 00:09:57.970
Rikudo Uni.

00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.110
That's it.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:02.920
I didn't notice at the Tokyo Sport track meet,

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:05.030
but matching uniforms are nice.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:09.820
When a bunch of guys wearing the same
color uniform are grouped up together,

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.090
it makes them look really strong.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:16.360
Yeah. And Rikudo's pure white
uniforms enhance the effect.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:19.010
It's like they're telling everyone
how strong they are.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.470
In contrast...

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:27.930
When we're not wearing our uniforms, 
you can't tell who we are.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:28.940
Yeah.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.110
You five, start jogging.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:36.080
It won't be as hot as the weather report said.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:38.320
We've got a chance.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:45.040
<b>42nd 
Kikui University 
Track and Field Meet</b>

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:45.040
<b>No 
unauthorized 
access to field
</b>Kikui University

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:41.760
All athletes participating in the 5000m race,

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:44.360
please gather at the starting line.

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:47.550
All athletes participating in the 5000m race,

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.240
please gather at the starting line.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:54.300
It's our second time, but I'm still nervous.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.330
It's because it's our second time.

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.720
Practice should be just as hard.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:02.280
Will we ever get used to this?

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:04.820
We probably shouldn't.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.430
Nicely said.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.710
I'm taking the inside.

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:11.870
Then I'll create space in front of you.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:14.150
Pass me if you think you've got it.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.380
Okay.

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.350
This kind of feels like a game.

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:19.150
Huh? Isn't this a game?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:21.110
No, like a soccer game.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.920
Oh, yeah. We used to swap
positions all the time.

00:11:24.920 --> 00:11:27.570
Our opponents couldn't tell us apart.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.440
I think I like games.

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:33.350
Me, too.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:36.540
I'm pretty nervous.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:39.260
They'll be fine. They're the elite team.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.960
<i>I'm running. I'm going to run.</i>

00:11:45.860 --> 00:11:48.300
I registered in advance.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:50.660
Then what have I been training for?

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:52.960
To run at Hakone.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:55.680
You already got your official record.

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.650
That's not what this is about!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.940
You should understand better than anyone

00:12:00.260 --> 00:12:03.320
how it feels not to be able
to run when you want to!

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.390
I do understand.

00:12:11.390 --> 00:12:14.000
I know you want to run more than anything.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.210
And that you don't see what running is about.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:17.670
What?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:21.040
Stop. Take in the view.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:24.060
Then slowly start running again.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.940
Be like Prince and Nico-chan Senpai.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:41.280
<b>Why?</b>

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:40.320
I don't think I've narrowly escaped.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.030
If anything, you could say
I've got no way out now.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.610
That was...

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:51.270
Oh, right. I heard you said something to Prince.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.180
You're a first-year, right?

00:12:53.180 --> 00:12:54.180
King.

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.170
That was...

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:00.880
It was the heat of the moment.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.130
So you take it back.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:07.080
I don't. I'm taking this seriously in my own way.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.570
You finally said what's really on your mind.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.770
I'm not blaming you.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:22.960
I can't believe I'm watching a track meet.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.650
I wouldn't have imagined this a month ago.

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.860
Watching them from here 
makes you realize how fast they are.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:51.880
To achieve an official record,
your pace for each lap needs to be...

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.470
Faster than 1:19.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:59.350
Last time, running took so much of my energy

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:02.770
that I couldn't afford to worry about my time.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.370
They're starting to spread out.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.560
Wow! The twins are hanging on!

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:37.110
They might actually do it.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.050
Musa, this is the moment of truth!

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:42.590
Calm down and hold that pace!

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:45.370
How many seconds per lap did you say?

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:49.320
Huh? Uh, one minute... um...

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.260
I forgot.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.250
Hey, you were smug when 
you immediately answered earlier!

00:14:53.250 --> 00:14:56.770
Shut up! It's your fault for not remembering!

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:07.850
Go! Go!

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:09.480
Aotake!

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:10.860
You can do it!

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:12.590
Go!

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:15.250
Aotake!

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.780
Keep it up! Keep it up!

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.280
Final lap!

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.290
Final lap!

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:22.450
Final lap!

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.420
Final lap!

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.950
Go! Go! Go!

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:31.100
Keep it up!

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:02.520
That was close.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:05.130
I thought you were gonna make it.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:06.930
You're unbelievable.

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:09.840
Wasn't that your best time, Yuki?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:13.580
You didn't achieve an official result,
but it wasn't bad, at all.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:16.250
When I think about how I have to run again,

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.880
it makes me want to puke.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:21.030
That was close.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:23.630
I waited too long during the middle.

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:25.730
I could've gone sooner.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.770
I realized I'm not someone
who can win a sprint.

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:33.740
You sound like a long-distance runner.

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:39.020
I laughed.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:40.160
Me, too.

00:17:40.730 --> 00:17:44.180
During our final lap, Haiji...

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:58.950
We couldn't hear what you 
were saying, but we saw you.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.780
Just as we were thinking,
"Stop! It's embarrassing,"

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:03.950
we actually started running faster.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:04.810
I know what you mean.

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:10.900
Support is really, truly essential.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:18.750
Just thinking that these two
were saying something to me

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:20.290
made my vision blurry.

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:22.890
Thank you.

00:18:22.890 --> 00:18:23.760
What?

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.160
I could see you.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.170
You were saying something, weren't you?

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:32.450
Musa's got really good eyes.

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:36.600
Yeah. He can see Aotake
from the top of the Skytree.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.420
Don't lie.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:42.260
He was calling everyone's names.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.890
S-So were you.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:47.350
I was just barely speaking.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:49.530
He was shouting.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:50.820
That's not fair.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.930
I was so embarrassed
to be standing next to him.

00:18:53.930 --> 00:18:56.130
I didn't know what to do.

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:02.060
He's a good guy at heart, too.

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.030
Hey.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:09.500
Everyone who ran and everyone
who cheered, you guys did a great job.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:13.900
Because of your efforts, 
everyone's times improved considerably.

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:16.520
This is a huge step forward.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:22.100
We've got our own way 
of doing things. Have faith.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.200
We'll have plenty more chances.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.100
Yes, sir!

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.230
You scared me.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:33.440
Well, it's not my style to end on a loss.

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:36.400
Oh, yeah? Should we run home, then?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.110
No way.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:42.710
I wish I could've been a spectator this time.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.910
Cheers!

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:53.520
How was it?

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.380
Huh?

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.070
Watching from the outside.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:59.880
Did you see anyone running half-assed?

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.660
I didn't see anyone.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.050
Everyone was going as hard as they could.

00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:10.770
Not just us. Everyone running was.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:17.380
I understand what you're trying to say.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:21.530
When they failed to achieve official records,

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:23.700
I was as disappointed as if it were me.

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:29.680
I felt for the first time the earnestness
of the people cheering around me.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:33.620
That's why I understand
what you're trying to say.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:38.380
